HELP=<<END
Run a bounded standalone Delta connector check from CAOS. This does not run the Delta application or execute agent turns. Requires a delta-runner-credentials secret containing this connector's account and actor identity. Never put credentials in arguments.
@param {string} request-id Fresh value so the check makes a real network exchange.
@param {string} [op] probe (default), inspect-history, replay-history, inspect-workspaces, bridge-context, or check-model. bridge-context imports an allowlisted thread into a CAOS session without inference. check-model checks this connector's default organization model-token authorization without inference. Neither edits Delta.
@param {string} [registration-name] Temporarily register, then clear, a diagnostic machine name.
@param {string} [thread-id] History to inspect; must be allowlisted in the sealed credential bundle. Only counts, never thread content or pack URLs, are returned.
END
IMAGE=run --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/flake-builder --in:@=. --lock:@=DEEP-DEPS/flake.lock
AGENT=curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/agent
PUBLISHER=curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/result-publisher
curry --base=$IMAGE --help=$HELP --agent-image=$AGENT --result-publisher=$PUBLISHER
